1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:06,000
Next, let's make the skirt.

2
00:00:06,000 --> 00:00:10,000
The skirt is to support the outer skirt structure,

3
00:00:10,000 --> 00:00:13,000
to make the structure more three-dimensional.

4
00:00:13,000 --> 00:00:15,000
Use the rectangle tool,

5
00:00:15,000 --> 00:00:18,000
click and drag in the 2D window,

6
00:00:18,000 --> 00:00:22,000
draw a rectangle that is twice as wide as the belt.

7
00:00:22,000 --> 00:00:26,000
Its length is the length of the skirt we will make later.

8
00:00:26,000 --> 00:00:29,000
Then we press Shift F to open the arrangement,

9
00:00:29,000 --> 00:00:32,000
arrange these two skirt panels on the side of the thigh,

10
00:00:32,000 --> 00:00:34,000
and then to the attribute editor,

11
00:00:34,000 --> 00:00:36,000
make the frame wider,

12
00:00:36,000 --> 00:00:38,000
so that the panel and the body do not have a gap.

13
00:00:38,000 --> 00:00:40,000
Then switch to the line pattern tool,

14
00:00:40,000 --> 00:00:42,000
click the panel outline,

15
00:00:42,000 --> 00:00:44,000
create the skirt and waist,

16
00:00:44,000 --> 00:00:46,000
and the skirt itself,

17
00:00:46,000 --> 00:00:49,000
its front and back pattern lines.

18
00:00:49,000 --> 00:00:51,000
Open the control key to simulate.

19
00:00:51,000 --> 00:00:52,000
After the simulation,

20
00:00:52,000 --> 00:00:55,000
we will see that the skirt panel is already worn on the body.

21
00:00:55,000 --> 00:00:57,000
In the 3D draft menu,

22
00:00:57,000 --> 00:00:59,000
we can find the line pattern,

23
00:00:59,000 --> 00:01:01,000
and the frame display.

24
00:01:01,000 --> 00:01:03,000
When we turn on the frame display,

25
00:01:03,000 --> 00:01:06,000
we can see the grid distribution on the panel.

26
00:01:06,000 --> 00:01:09,000
It can be seen that when the particle diameter is 20,

27
00:01:09,000 --> 00:01:11,000
the grid is relatively small.

28
00:01:11,000 --> 00:01:13,000
If we reduce the particle diameter to 10,

29
00:01:13,000 --> 00:01:15,000
because the grid is more,

30
00:01:15,000 --> 00:01:18,000
its overall simulation is more detailed,

31
00:01:18,000 --> 00:01:20,000
and it will make the panel look softer.

32
00:01:20,000 --> 00:01:22,000
We can also reduce the impact thickness,

33
00:01:22,000 --> 00:01:25,000
and reduce the air thickness between the panel and other panels.

34
00:01:25,000 --> 00:01:27,000
Then we can return to the thick texture surface.

35
00:01:27,000 --> 00:01:28,000
Only in the thick texture surface,

36
00:01:28,000 --> 00:01:31,000
under the clothing display style,

37
00:01:31,000 --> 00:01:34,000
we can see the thickness of the panel.

38
00:01:34,000 --> 00:01:37,000
If you don't think there are enough folds here,

39
00:01:37,000 --> 00:01:39,000
we can widen the skirt panel,

40
00:01:39,000 --> 00:01:41,000
but after widening,

41
00:01:41,000 --> 00:01:44,000
because our grid is increased according to the original trend,

42
00:01:44,000 --> 00:01:47,000
so there may be a difference in the back.

43
00:01:47,000 --> 00:01:49,000
So we can right-click on the panel,

44
00:01:49,000 --> 00:01:52,000
select Rearrange 3D Arrangement Position,

45
00:01:52,000 --> 00:01:54,000
to rearrange the panel,

46
00:01:54,000 --> 00:01:56,000
return it to the time when it was just arranged,

47
00:01:56,000 --> 00:01:58,000
and then start to simulate again.

48
00:01:58,000 --> 00:01:59,000
After the simulation,

49
00:01:59,000 --> 00:02:01,000
if there are some differences,

50
00:02:01,000 --> 00:02:04,000
we can give this skirt a level.

51
00:02:04,000 --> 00:02:07,000
Because other panels have levels of 0,

52
00:02:07,000 --> 00:02:09,000
so we apply a level of 1 to the skirt,

53
00:02:09,000 --> 00:02:11,000
and it will naturally pass to the outside.

54
00:02:11,000 --> 00:02:12,000
After the simulation is stable,

55
00:02:12,000 --> 00:02:14,000
we return the level to 0.

56
00:02:14,000 --> 00:02:16,000
Here we will see that there is a difference in the belt,

57
00:02:16,000 --> 00:02:19,000
because we modified the skirt panel that we sewed together with it.

58
00:02:19,000 --> 00:02:22,000
So here we apply a level of 1 to the belt,

59
00:02:22,000 --> 00:02:23,000
and re-simulate it.

60
00:02:23,000 --> 00:02:25,000
After re-activating the simulation,

61
00:02:25,000 --> 00:02:26,000
we will see that the skirt white

62
00:02:26,000 --> 00:02:29,000
is a little bit deformed.

63
00:02:29,000 --> 00:02:31,000
So when we select the belt,

64
00:02:31,000 --> 00:02:34,000
we click on the fabric window to apply the new fabric.

65
00:02:34,000 --> 00:02:36,000
For the new one,

66
00:02:36,000 --> 00:02:38,000
we only use the fabric on the belt,

67
00:02:38,000 --> 00:02:40,000
we need to improve its gold tail,

68
00:02:40,000 --> 00:02:41,000
sand strength,

69
00:02:41,000 --> 00:02:42,000
and the tension of the corner line.

70
00:02:42,000 --> 00:02:44,000
These three values are the stretch performance

71
00:02:44,000 --> 00:02:47,000
of the gold tail and the corner line of the panel.

72
00:02:47,000 --> 00:02:48,000
The higher these three values,

73
00:02:48,000 --> 00:02:50,000
the more difficult it is for the fabric to stretch,

74
00:02:50,000 --> 00:02:53,000
so even if the skirt panel is very large,

75
00:02:53,000 --> 00:02:55,000
it will not affect the belt panel,

76
00:02:55,000 --> 00:02:56,000
and it will not be deformed.

77
00:02:56,000 --> 00:02:58,000
If you want the fabric to stretch more easily,

78
00:02:58,000 --> 00:02:59,000
you can set it in reverse.

79
00:02:59,000 --> 00:03:01,000
Next, let's learn

80
00:03:01,000 --> 00:03:04,000
what effects the bending strength will have.

81
00:03:04,000 --> 00:03:06,000
Here we select the skirt panel,

82
00:03:06,000 --> 00:03:07,000
click on the Shift key,

83
00:03:07,000 --> 00:03:08,000
you can choose more,

84
00:03:08,000 --> 00:03:11,000
apply them to a new piece of fabric.

85
00:03:11,000 --> 00:03:13,000
When the bending strength is higher,

86
00:03:13,000 --> 00:03:15,000
the whole fabric will become harder.

87
00:03:15,000 --> 00:03:17,000
In this case,

88
00:03:17,000 --> 00:03:19,000
the number of folds will decrease,

89
00:03:19,000 --> 00:03:22,000
and the single fold will become larger and wider,

90
00:03:22,000 --> 00:03:24,000
and it will look thicker.

91
00:03:24,000 --> 00:03:27,000
And the panel itself has a certain support.

92
00:03:27,000 --> 00:03:30,000
When the bending strength of the panel is lowered,

93
00:03:30,000 --> 00:03:32,000
it looks softer,

94
00:03:32,000 --> 00:03:33,000
not so hard,

95
00:03:33,000 --> 00:03:37,000
and its overall elasticity looks better.

96
00:03:37,000 --> 00:03:38,000
Then we press Ctrl C

97
00:03:38,000 --> 00:03:41,000
to return to the bending strength of the modification.

98
00:03:41,000 --> 00:03:43,000
We first activate the inner layer of the clothing,

99
00:03:43,000 --> 00:03:46,000
let it be simulated with other panels,

100
00:03:46,000 --> 00:03:49,000
and we return the excess layers to 0.

101
00:03:49,000 --> 00:03:50,000
Because the frozen panel,

102
00:03:50,000 --> 00:03:52,000
it will maintain its own shape,

103
00:03:52,000 --> 00:03:53,000
and after the deflation,

104
00:03:53,000 --> 00:03:55,000
we need to simulate it first,

105
00:03:55,000 --> 00:03:57,000
to prevent some conflicts and instability

106
00:03:57,000 --> 00:04:01,000
caused by too many panels being deflated at the same time.

107
00:04:01,000 --> 00:04:02,000
After the simulation is stable,

108
00:04:02,000 --> 00:04:05,000
we can freeze the top again.

109
00:04:05,000 --> 00:04:07,000
For the skirt of the lower body,

110
00:04:07,000 --> 00:04:09,000
if you think its length is too short,

111
00:04:09,000 --> 00:04:13,000
we can directly drag the selection frame of the selected panel

112
00:04:13,000 --> 00:04:15,000
and lengthen its skirt.

113
00:04:15,000 --> 00:04:18,000
Note that we are stretching down,

114
00:04:18,000 --> 00:04:19,000
stretching down.

115
00:04:19,000 --> 00:04:21,000
Of course, you can use the adjustment panel tool

116
00:04:21,000 --> 00:04:22,000
or the edit panel tool

117
00:04:22,000 --> 00:04:25,000
to drag the bottom down.

118
00:04:25,000 --> 00:04:26,000
When you are stretching,

119
00:04:26,000 --> 00:04:28,000
don't stretch it too much at a time,

120
00:04:28,000 --> 00:04:30,000
otherwise the grid will extend along the original shape,

121
00:04:30,000 --> 00:04:33,000
and it may have some conflicts and instability.

122
00:04:33,000 --> 00:04:34,000
If you want to shorten it,

123
00:04:34,000 --> 00:04:35,000
it is the same,

124
00:04:35,000 --> 00:04:37,000
pull the bottom up here.

125
00:04:37,000 --> 00:04:40,000
Remember to simulate every time you modify the panel,

126
00:04:40,000 --> 00:04:42,000
and let them modify it.

127
00:04:42,000 --> 00:04:44,000
As a group,

128
00:04:44,000 --> 00:04:47,000
because we can't see the wrinkles inside it,

129
00:04:47,000 --> 00:04:50,000
so you can also reduce the number of wrinkles

130
00:04:50,000 --> 00:04:51,000
according to the need.

131
00:04:51,000 --> 00:04:53,000
To reduce the number of wrinkles,

132
00:04:53,000 --> 00:04:54,000
it is very simple,

133
00:04:54,000 --> 00:04:57,000
just shrink the panel.

134
00:05:04,000 --> 00:05:06,000
As we did the tie part before,

135
00:05:06,000 --> 00:05:09,000
because later we will add another layer of skirt

136
00:05:09,000 --> 00:05:10,000
on the outside of the skirt,

137
00:05:10,000 --> 00:05:13,000
so we first use a relatively low

138
00:05:13,000 --> 00:05:15,000
end-to-end shrink rate for these two panels

139
00:05:15,000 --> 00:05:16,000
to shrink it up.

140
00:05:16,000 --> 00:05:18,000
If there are still some wrinkles,

141
00:05:18,000 --> 00:05:20,000
we will reduce the end-to-end shrink rate a little more,

142
00:05:20,000 --> 00:05:23,000
so that it looks like there are no wrinkles on the surface,

143
00:05:23,000 --> 00:05:25,000
and make the structure of the outer layer.

144
00:05:25,000 --> 00:05:28,000
Then we can freeze all the panels.

